### Schinagl, S., & Shahim, A. (2020)

**Full citation:** Schinagl, S., & Shahim, A. (2020). What do we know about information security governance? Re-conceptualisation through a systematic literature review. *Information and Computer Security*, *28*(2), 261–292.  
**Role:** Contrasting position — ISG coherence assumption  
**Claim:** ISG scholarship treats external regulatory mandates as coherent boundary conditions that organisations internalise — it has not theorised multi-regulator mandate incoherence as a structural source of governance burden.  
**Where used:** §2.2 (ISG coherence assumption that P3 challenges)

